<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		The returned skeletal xenotype gains Alpha Genes' heat and cold immunity.

		Gating, which is why this is its own folder: VU_ReturnedSkeletal is not a Yokai or Vampires-and-the-Undead def
		at all. Big and Small - Genes & More defines it, inside a folder that its own loadFolders only loads when one
		of RedMattis.Undead, RedMattis.Yokai or RedMattis.Undead.ZombieApoc is active. This folder mirrors that exact
		condition, which also covers the zombie apocalypse submod that the original's check missed.

		Worth a look later: the xenotype already carries MaxTemp_HugeIncrease and MinTemp_HugeDecrease, and this adds
		the Alpha Genes immunities on top without removing them. The equivalent Yokai patches (kitsune, great red oni)
		do remove the B&S genes when adding the Alpha Genes one, so the two are inconsistent.

		Fix 2026-10-18: each immunity is added only when the xenotype lacks it. MMMM Convergence - Genetics swaps
		MaxTemp_HugeIncrease / MinTemp_HugeDecrease for these same genes everywhere; when Convergence loaded first, this
		add then listed both immunities twice ("Hyperlink to AG_ColdImmunity more than once"). Any load order works now.
	-->
	<!--
		The mod gate sits on an <li> inside a sequence, not on the <Operation> itself: RimWorld reads
		MayRequire only on list elements, so an <Operation MayRequire="..."> node loads and applies
		unconditionally. Do not flatten this wrapper away.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="sarg.alphagenes">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
						<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_ReturnedSkeletal"]/genes[not(li[text()="AG_HeatImmunity"])]</xpath>
						<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
							<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_ReturnedSkeletal"]/genes</xpath>
							<value>
								<li>AG_HeatImmunity</li>
							</value>
						</match>
					</li>
					<li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
						<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_ReturnedSkeletal"]/genes[not(li[text()="AG_ColdImmunity"])]</xpath>
						<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
							<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_ReturnedSkeletal"]/genes</xpath>
							<value>
								<li>AG_ColdImmunity</li>
							</value>
						</match>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>
</Patch>
